  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Vetjet Fuels has $349M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Vetjet Fuels won 288 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are up 100.9% year over year. Obligations increased across recent fiscal years: FY21 $2.7M, FY22 $4.1M, FY23 $9.4M, FY24 $69M, and FY25 $174M, leading to FY26 $349M. The Department of Defense is the primary buyer in FY2026 to date, accounting for $349M in obligations. Petroleum Refineries is the primary NAICS market in FY2026 to date, accounting for $349M in obligations. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. Award-value tables and expiring-contract tables use total contract values rather than obligation flows. This summary highlights obligation totals, buyer concentration, market concentration, and the multi-year growth pattern through FY26 to give contracting officers and business development teams a clear, numbers-first snapshot of Vetjet Fuels in the federal market.",
